{
  "description": "Routing a write to one of an owner's sibling shards by a caller-supplied key (stable partitioning). Rendezvous (highest-random-weight) hashing: for each candidate shard id the weight is SHA-256 of the preimage 'avalon-shard-route-v1' (UTF-8 tag, no length) followed by the owner, the key and the shard id, each as a u32 big-endian UTF-8 byte length then the bytes. The candidate with the greatest weight, compared as 32 big-endian bytes, wins. Candidates are first reduced to the unique ids that are members of the owner's family (shard-family-head.json memberVectors); equal weights can only come from equal ids, so the tie-break is the bytewise smaller shard id and duplicates collapse. No candidates left means no route (shardId null). Adding or removing a sibling moves only the keys whose winner is that sibling. The key is hashed as its UTF-8 bytes with no Unicode normalisation. This is client-side only: the server does not route writes, and nothing here makes writes across siblings atomic.",
  "generation": "Deterministic; produced by an independent implementation (SHA-256 over the stated preimage), not by any SDK.",
  "supportedIn": [
    "rust",
    "csharp",
    "typescript"
  ],
